      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Count and fetch can observe different database snapshots",
      "description": "The count and fetch run on the same connection, but under PostgreSQL\u2019s default `READ COMMITTED` isolation, each statement gets a new snapshot. A concurrent insert after the count can make the fetch return more rows than `max_rows`, contrary to the reader module\u2019s claim that the race can only produce an over-ceiling response. The handler does not validate the fetched row count, so the API can return an oversized response despite its admission guard. Use a consistent snapshot for both statements or enforce the ceiling against the fetched result. The same issue applies to the trades handler at lines 153\u2013166.",
